here's what happened when I was working  on Saturday Night Live with Albert  Brooks it was the late 70s and I was  always a fan of music a big fan of rock  and roll and just then that whole punk  rock movement started happening and I  started going out and seeing all the  bands and going to the clubs and under  striding to understand this movement  which to me was very very radical music  movement but also radical social  movement and I and I really think about  myself I didn't really consciously say  it back then but today I think about  myself as kind of a rock and roll  anthropologist and I I wanted to learn  more about the the punk rock scene and  all the guys I was working with when I  was hanging out with Albert  you know like Rob Reiner and Oh James  Brooks and you know a lot of really  high-profile comedians they said they  you know  Penelope go on an interview you maybe  you could produce this movie Private  Benjamin that Goldie Hawn is doing and I  said no I think I'm not even going to go  on that interview because I had just  produced real life Albert Brooks first  feature I said now I'm not even gonna go  on that interview because I want to make  a documentary on punk rock music and  they all thought I was crazy and matter  of fact they they harassed me a lot  about it but I went and did it anyway  and it was really it was the decline of  Western civilization is the first  feature I did and it was some people say  the most written about movie of that  year which would have been 1981 when it  was released and everyone was writing  about that movie because they didn't  understand the movement all the critics  all the reviewers they just had to  understand it and know it and see it and  try to figure it out so it really put me  on the map as a director now the thing  about doing the decline of Western  civilization which to me that was the  point in my career what I decided I'm  not going to be a producer I'm going to  be a director I I to this day and so  thankful that I made that decision  because making movies is all  about changing people's lives and so  many people over the years have come to  me and said thank you for making the  decline of Western civilization series  there's three films now because it  changed my life it made me think  differently about the world it made me  move out here from you know Hoboken or  you know it made a big difference in a  lot of people's lives and if there's any  real one reason for making a movie it's  if you can change people's lives  you
 

